Mikael Kalms' C2P collection - licence

The routines in this directory are Public Domain. From the upstream readme.txt
(kept here unchanged):

  All files except in the "others" directory are Public Domain: Anyone can
  do as they please with the code, feel free to use it for non-commercial
  as well as commercial purposes, change and redistribute the contents
  as you please.

Each vendored .s file repeats this in its own header ("This routine is
released into the public domain. It may be freely used for non-commercial as
well as commercial purposes."). Nothing from the upstream "others" directory is
vendored. Public Domain code may be included in this MIT-licensed project
without conditions; the credit to Mikael Kalms (mikael@kalms.org) is kept as a
courtesy, and the author asks for a short notice by email when the code is used.
